<%# locals: (sources: true, projects: true) %>
<%#
  WHERE FILES COME FROM, AND WHAT A Projects/ FOLDER BECOMES (F onboarding, 2026-10-13). ONE
  definition of both sentences, rendered by Recent's getting-started panel, the Library's empty
  state and the Projects page's, so the three cannot drift about what this deployment does.

  ASKED OF `capabilities`, NEVER OF AN ADAPTER CLASS: scannable means a poll fills the catalog
  (share, s3), presignable is what tells a bucket from a folder, and syncable means the desktop
  app. Every timing here is a schedule in config/recurring.yml: library_scan, project_discovery and
  project_folder_intake all run every 15 minutes, and a scan runs discovery and the filing sweep
  inline (Library::ScanJob#perform), so a scannable library's new folder is a project, and its loose
  files filed, within one scan.

  The share sentence's subject comes from LibraryFolderHelper#library_folder_label: three states by
  LIBRARY_HOST_PATH (absent, empty, set), display-only.

  THE FILING SENTENCE NAMES ITS EXCEPTIONS because the sweep moves files: a README at a project's
  root is never filed, and nothing inside a git working tree is (Maker::AttachToProject's
  refusals; docs/invariants/project-intake.md). A sentence that over-promised a move would be the
  one place this copy could frighten someone into moving their own repository.

  PARAGRAPHS, NOT A BULLETED LIST: the Library and Projects render this inside an empty-state box,
  which centres its text, and the tools first-run state is the precedent for that box holding
  paragraphs. `sources:` and `projects:` let Recent put the two halves under two numbered steps.
%>
<% if sources %>
  <div class="file-sources">
    <p><strong>Upload</strong>, in the top bar, puts files from this computer in the folder you
      are viewing, or in one you choose.</p>
    <% if capabilities.scannable? %>
      <% if capabilities.presignable? %>
        <p><strong>The storage bucket</strong> this server uses is your library. Files another
          program or a sync tool puts there appear here within 15 minutes, or right away with
          Rescan library, under More actions (⋯) on the <%= link_to "Library", files_path %> page.</p>
      <% else %>
        <p><strong><%= library_folder_label %></strong> is your library. Anything put there,
          over a NAS share, by another program or by a plain copy, appears here within 15 minutes,
          or right away with Rescan library, under More actions (⋯) on the
          <%= link_to "Library", files_path %> page.</p>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <% if capabilities.syncable? %>
      <p><strong>The desktop app</strong> keeps a folder on your computer in sync with this
        library; what you save there appears here within a few minutes.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
<% if projects %>
  <p class="projects-intake">A folder directly inside <code>Projects/</code>, at the top of the
    library, becomes a project within 15 minutes. Files left loose at the top of a project's folder
    are then filed into type folders such as <code>models/</code> and <code>docs/</code>, except a
    README and anything in a git repository; your
    <%= link_to "Filing", settings_filing_rules_path %> settings decide which type goes where.</p>
<% end %>
